WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:04.055
Roscoe and Cleo walked down Main Street.

2
00:00:04.056 --> 00:00:07.199
The town was peaceful.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.888
But out west things don't stay peaceful for long.

4
00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:16.305
Annie came around a corner, carrying a basket.

5
00:00:16.306 --> 00:00:18.450
Oswald was with her.

6
00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:22.733
Annie smiled at the sheriff. "Nice morning, isn't it?"

7
00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:26.912
"Not as nice as you!" Roscoe thought.

8
00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:32.293
As usual, that dog was too lovestruck to speak.

9
00:00:32.294 --> 00:00:35.119
All he could do was nod.

10
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.361
Cleo slapped a paw over her mouth to hide her smile.

11
00:00:39.362 --> 00:00:43.030
"We're going to the general store," Oswald said.

12
00:00:43.031 --> 00:00:48.033
"Miss Annie's getting candy for the class."

13
00:00:48.034 --> 00:00:51.716
Roscoe tipped his hat as they walked away.

14
00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:55.877
He let out a sigh.

15
00:00:55.878 --> 00:00:58.495
Cleo grinned at Roscoe.

16
00:00:58.496 --> 00:01:01.730
"We could use a few things from the store too."

17
00:01:01.731 --> 00:01:08.948
"Great idea!" Roscoe took off after Annie and Oswald.

18
00:01:08.949 --> 00:01:16.112
Cleo had to run to catch up.

19
00:01:16.113 --> 00:01:19.987
Inside the store Annie stood at the counter.

20
00:01:19.988 --> 00:01:24.630
Sam, the owner, scooped gumdrops into a small bag.

21
00:01:24.631 --> 00:01:27.265
He handed the bag to Miss Annie.

22
00:01:27.266 --> 00:01:31.208
"Sweets for our sweet schoolteacher," Sam said.

23
00:01:31.209 --> 00:01:37.270
He laughed at his own joke.

24
00:01:37.271 --> 00:01:42.940
Roscoe frowned. "Who does this crow think he is?" he thought.

25
00:01:42.941 --> 00:01:46.022
"Let's hurry, Oswald," Annie said.

26
00:01:46.023 --> 00:01:49.039
"It's almost time for school to start."

27
00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.618
Roscoe cleared his throat.

28
00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:55.013
"Have a nice day, Miss Annie."

29
00:01:55.014 --> 00:02:00.189
Annie smiled. "Same to you, Sheriff. Good-bye, Cleo."

30
00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:03.635
She and Oswald left.

31
00:02:03.636 --> 00:02:08.359
Roscoe puffed out his chest, feeling quite pleased with himself.

32
00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.697
He just spoke to Miss Annie.

33
00:02:10.698 --> 00:02:13.943
And she smiled back at him!

34
00:02:13.944 --> 00:02:17.396
"Good morning, Sheriff," Sam said.

35
00:02:17.397 --> 00:02:19.723
"What can I get you?"

36
00:02:19.724 --> 00:02:23.034
"We need cheese and crackers, Sam," Roscoe said.

37
00:02:23.035 --> 00:02:29.462
Cleo yawned. "And coffee beans."

38
00:02:29.463 --> 00:02:34.739
She and Roscoe leaned on the counter while Sam gathered items.

39
00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.800
He came back with some crackers and cheese.

40
00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:43.589
Then he filled a bag with coffee beans.

41
00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:48.052
"Thanks, Sam." Cleo handed him some coins.

42
00:02:48.053 --> 00:02:51.257
Just then the door burst open.

43
00:02:51.258 --> 00:02:54.023
Two raccoons ran inside.

44
00:02:54.024 --> 00:02:59.713
"Grab some tomatoes, Rocky!" one raccoon said.

45
00:02:59.714 --> 00:03:05.121
Rocky laughed. "Don't forget eggs, Gus!"

46
00:03:05.122 --> 00:03:07.264
Sam groaned.

47
00:03:07.265 --> 00:03:11.415
"It's the Tomato Brothers! They're always causing trouble!"

48
00:03:11.416 --> 00:03:18.421
The raccoons hurried around, hooting and laughing.

49
00:03:18.422 --> 00:03:23.692
They filled their arms with eggs, tomatoes, and other vegetables.

50
00:03:23.693 --> 00:03:26.429
Roscoe kept an eye on them.

51
00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.832
"Those raccoons sure seem like trouble," he thought.

52
00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:32.299
"But they aren't breaking any laws."

53
00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.492
That changed mighty fast though.

54
00:03:35.493 --> 00:03:39.256
Those raccoons ran out without paying!

55
00:03:39.257 --> 00:03:42.248
"They're stealing!" Sam shouted.

56
00:03:42.249 --> 00:03:45.000
Roscoe and Cleo rushed outside.

57
00:03:45.001 --> 00:03:49.005
"Stop right there!" Roscoe yelled.

58
00:03:49.006 --> 00:03:53.979
To Roscoe's surprise, the raccoons did stop.

59
00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:57.061
Roscoe reached for his handcuffs.

60
00:03:57.062 --> 00:04:03.961
Splat! A tomato hit him in the face!

